<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Changing the Subject 3 - Kinetic energy</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The kinetic energy \(E\) of an object of mass \(m\) moving with speed \(v\) is given by \(E = \frac{1}{2}mv^2\).</p>
<p>(a) Make \(v\) the subject of the formula (take \(v > 0\)).</p>
<p>\(v = \) [[input:ans1]]  [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]] </p>
<p>(b) Find \(v\) in m/s when \(E = {@nE@}\) J and \(m = {@nm@}\) kg.</p>
<p>\(v = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Multiply both sides by 2: \(2E = mv^2\).</p>
<p>Divide both sides by \(m\): \(v^2 = \frac{2E}{m}\).</p>
<p>Take the square root of both sides: \(v = \sqrt{\frac{2E}{m}}\).</p>
<p>Substituting: \(v = \sqrt{\frac{2({@nE@})}{ {@nm@} }} = {@nv@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
